	"bugClass": {
		"id": "premature-secret-persistence",
		"title": "Persisting credentials before signup preflight completes",
		"cause": "A credential-generation workflow stores a newly created persistent secret before validating the reviewed form or confirming that the destination/action still matches. If nonsecret input changes the action, the secret is not submitted, but the create-only credential remains orphaned.",
		"criteria": "Include a site when a password or other generated persistent secret is saved before form validation or destination/action preflight completes, leaving a credential behind when validation fails or the action changes. Either ordering failure qualifies independently: saving before remaining form validation, or saving before confirming the destination/action. Exclude flows where persistence occurs only after the reviewed form and destination preflight succeed.",
